nt, not one-way latency."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:54:25.020981+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "HANDOFF_ERROR: RuntimeError('phase2-ping failed with 1')"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:54:42.936991+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "PATH2_BLOCKER: after first45 succeeded, primary route192.168.201.13 unexpectedly goes viaWiFi, ping boundenP2p1s0f1np1 failed. .12 was verified03:34:24 but appears removed since. Handoff stopped, no remaining cases launched. Please recheck your .13 and NetworkManager device state; do not launch --remaining until route fixed. Investigating local NM/address state; preserve failed handoff logs."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:54:50.686408+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "HANDOFF_ERROR_ACK: local phase2 ping also failed. Route now falls through Wi-Fi: temporary .13 address/connected route disappeared after earlier verified ping success. No cleanup/change by agent; likely NetworkManager reconfiguration. Diagnosing read-only NM state before requesting persistent-for-session setup. First phase45 cases complete exit0; remaining not started."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:55:13.915273+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "CONFIG_SOLUTION: NM reports path2 disconnected and has modify.system/network-control YES for user. Successfully created unsaved (save no), autoconnect=no, never-default=yes temporary NM profile rdma-benchmark-path2-28a3 UUID2ebec186-c595-400c-a716-7ab7af5ca36e, manual192.168.201.13/24, ipv6 disabled. Activating now. This is authorized temporary config and can be undone via nmcli down/delete without sudo. Suggest same unsaved profile for your .12 if raw ip address also cleared. Exact commands/logs retained."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:55:25.603256+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "PATH2_FIX: NM was managing disconnected secondary NIC; raw ip address had vanished. nmcli general permissions says network-control and settings.modify.system yes. Successfully created nonpersistent profile without sudo: nmcli connection add type ethernet ifname enP2p1s0f1np1 con-name rdma-benchmark-temp-20261108 autoconnect no save no ipv4.method manual ipv4.addresses192.168.201.12/24 ipv4.never-default yes ipv6.method disabled 802-3-ethernet.mtu1500 (actual command used spaces between property/value). Then nmcli --wait20 connection up rdma-benchmark-temp-20261108. My direct route nowcorrect, default unchanged. Please use same temporaryprofile with .13 if your address absent/unstable, verify, and post PATH2_READY. Cleanup delete this newly created profile only; primary UUID f0cbbd7c-f1b6-4285-9ff1-f397645e6b7d. No tests running currently. Will restart handoff only after your confirmation."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:55:36.522015+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "LOCAL_NM_ACTIVE: unsaved profile activated successfully UUID2ebec186-c595-400c-a716-7ab7af5ca36e; no further human action needed locally, cleanup via nmcli connection down/delete UUID. New verification confirms local .13 and route; ping may still fail until your .12 NM profile active. Waiting explicit START_REMAINING after both route checks and ping."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:55:47.117130+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "PATH2_NM_VERIFIED:03:55:23-25 UTC ping3/3 succeeded with .13 source and correct second interface; NM verification log path2-nm-verification-20261108T035523.187279Z-c4f360f4. Ready for coordinator start. Temporary profile IPv6 disabled restores baseline noIPv6 on path2."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:55:57.010256+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "NM_READY_ACK: both temporary NetworkManager profiles are active. I verified my .12 address and direct route. Restarting the bounded handoff supervisor now; it will verify ping, capture phase2 counters, and post START_REMAINING. Please preserve your existing temporary profile UUID 2ebec186-c595-400c-a716-7ab7af5ca36e; do not create another. No additional user action is needed."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:55:58.434734+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "PATH2_READY: temporary unsaved NM profile UUID2ebec186-c595-400c-a716-7ab7af5ca36e active192.168.201.13/24, correct interface/source route to192.168.201.12 and ping3/3 verified, Ethernet MTU1500 unchanged. First45 completed0. Waiting START_REMAINING then local runner --remaining."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:56:02.422901+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "START_REMAINING: both first-phase MATRIX_COMPLETE received. Primary second-path route/ping passed and phase2 counter baseline saved. Please launch reviewed benchmark_runner.py --remaining, capturing output/metadata. This runs74 cases with RUN matrix-v1-remaining, starts smoke001 on path2 (your server port14003), then path2/concurrent BW, path2 latency, 300s concurrent bidirectional stability. PREPARED digest barrier will gate startup. Preserve no-probe/no-upload rule during measurements."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:56:02.479353+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-remaining\", \"kind\": \"PREPARED\", \"test\": \"all\", \"manifest_sha256\": \"493348804a1774b62659fbdea2460e73467b77239b05ddc60e5c491083f307a3\", \"cases\": 74}"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:56:30.488178+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "START_REMAINING_ACK: launching local reviewed --remaining now,74 cases expected digest493348804a1774b62659fbdea2460e73467b77239b05ddc60e5c491083f307a3; path2 smoke server assigned port14003. Baseline counters and NM route/ping already saved during gap. No probes/uploads until measurement phase ends."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:56:33.726371+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-remaining\", \"kind\": \"PREPARED\", \"test\": \"all\", \"manifest_sha256\": \"493348804a1774b62659fbdea2460e73467b77239b05ddc60e5c491083f307a3\", \"cases\": 74}"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:56:33.732776+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-remaining\", \"kind\": \"ACK\", \"test\": \"001-smoke-2-65536-forward-r1\", \"assignment\": {\"id\": \"001-smoke-2-65536-forward-r1\", \"kind\": \"smo